@title Observability Stack 2027
@subtitle Comparing Datadog, Grafana Cloud and a self-hosted stack
@author SRE team, Copperleaf Insurance

kpi Hosts | 340
kpi Logs ingested | 2.1 TB/month
kpi On-call engineers | 14

The options are Datadog, Grafana Cloud, and a self-hosted stack running Prometheus, Loki and Grafana on our own Kubernetes.

# Comparison table
table = Option,Setup effort,Alerting,Log search,Lock-in,Annual cost; Datadog,low,excellent,excellent,high,"$412,000"; Grafana Cloud,low,good,good,medium,"$236,000"; Self-hosted,high,good,fair,low,"$148,000 + 1.5 engineers"

# Three-year cost
data threeyear = year,Datadog,Grafana Cloud,Self-hosted; 2027,412,236,418; 2028,865,496,706; 2029,1363,782,1004
chart line threeyear unit=k$ focus="Grafana Cloud" title="Cumulative cost, thousands of dollars"

Self-hosted figures include staff time. Counted that way, Grafana Cloud stays cheapest in every year.

# Pros and cons
## Datadog
- Pro: excellent alerting and log search.
- Pro: low setup effort.
- Con: most expensive by a wide margin.
- Con: high lock-in.

## Grafana Cloud
- Pro: cheapest once staff time is counted.
- Pro: dashboards stay portable.
- Pro: low setup effort.
- Con: log search is good, not excellent.

## Self-hosted
- Pro: lowest lock-in.
- Pro: lowest license cost.
- Con: high setup effort and 1.5 engineers to run it.
- Con: fair log search.

# Recommendation
Choose **Grafana Cloud**. It is the cheapest option once staff time is counted, and it keeps our dashboards portable.

! The Datadog quote expires on 2026-11-30. Self-hosted assumes we can hire 1.5 engineers, which is not yet approved.
